WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.730
- Social media is filled with
all sorts of cool things.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.200
I enjoy bringing you my favorites.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.236
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.236 --> 00:00:08.040
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.290
Makeup tutorials have been a hot trend

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.940
on social media for a bit,

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.080
but one Connecticut woman

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.970
isn't just sharing her makeup tips.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.260
She actually throws down

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.050
some serious relationship
advice at the same time

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.620
which has earned her nearly 1
million followers on TikTok.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.540
- I talk about the 20
lessons on love and life

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.740
that I had to learn the hard way.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:26.760
Just because a man loves you

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.320
doesn't mean he wants
to be with you forever.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.520
Sometimes the person you want

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.020
is not the person you need to be with.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.160
If you need to make excuses

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.450
for why you should stay in a relationship,

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.920
it probably means you need to leave.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.300
You can be the best version of yourself

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.560
and still get rejected, and that's 'cause

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.480
not everyone appreciates
the same type of art.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.250
Always choose the man who
makes you feel at peace

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.360
rather than the man who makes you feel

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.380
like you're on a rollercoaster.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.460
The rollercoaster is exciting,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.840
but at some point you need to get off.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.100
If someone is telling you to settle,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.090
it probably means they didn't get

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.403
what they wanted in life and
don't wanna see you get yours.

00:00:50.403 --> 00:00:51.326
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:51.326 --> 00:00:54.087
- I love her. (chuckles)

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.520
And Anna says she's got the experience

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.230
to back up her words of wisdom.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:01.200
We've got her on the line
now watching on NBC New York.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.768
What's going on Anna?

00:01:02.768 --> 00:01:04.018
(audience claps and cheers)

00:01:04.018 --> 00:01:06.480
- Hi, great to see you.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.740
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.480
Well, first of all, you're hilarious.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.820
Secondly, you are stunningly beautiful.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.250
So how did you come up with
this creative combination

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.080
of beauty and romance?

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.090
- Well, growing up in Pennsylvania

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.760
in the 90s as an Asian American girl,

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.170
there weren't a lot of makeup artists

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.210
who knew how to do my face.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.430
So I taught myself how to do my own makeup

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.890
through a lot of trial and error.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.590
And of course the other
component to my stories

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:35.400
is my very checkered dating history.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:39.270
I probably went on at
least 200 first dates

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.730
in my twenties in New York

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:44.700
and have a lot of failed relationships

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.710
and a lot of stories as a result.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.510
And I put the two together,

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.670
not really thinking anything of it.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.260
Posted my first get ready with me

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.990
on September 1st of this last year.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.600
It went viral and I've done at least

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.700
50 get ready with me's since then.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:00.990
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.930
Your advice is hilarious
and also very true.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.370
So what's your best advice

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.370
and what's your relationship status now?

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.310
- I am married to my best friend

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.530
and I would've never met him-

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:14.370
- Congratulations.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.972
- [Anna] If it wasn't for
all the failed relationships.

00:02:15.972 --> 00:02:16.805
- Yeah.

00:02:16.805 --> 00:02:20.040
- I truly believe that failure

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.900
is such a critical component to growth.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.900
And I always tell people
that there is always a light

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.470
at the end of the tunnel if
we bring our own lighter.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:31.050
I think what I learned from my twenties

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.370
is that when you're young

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.260
and your life is blowing up in your face

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.940
and nothing's going according to plan,

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.860
everything feels like
the end of the world.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.500
But it's not, it is just the beginning.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.120
- Yeah, it's just a moment.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.470
You're right. You're right.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.580
Well, thank you so much

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.093
and I'm liking your post
right now, all right.

00:02:47.093 --> 00:02:47.926
(heart tings)

00:02:47.926 --> 00:02:49.410
(audience claps and cheers)

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.243
And that's not all.

00:02:50.243 --> 00:02:52.770
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.270
the go-to pen of the
"Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.100
want to celebrate truly unstoppable

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.810
and funny people just like you.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.000
So they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1000.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.833
How's that sound?

00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:02.640
(audience claps and cheers)

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.633
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.160
I'm gonna go buy a lot of
ice-cream now. (laughs)

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.330
- Thank you Anna.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.070
And thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:13.710
Brooke Shields, Echo Kellum, Chef Blondie,

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.660
Dr. Lauren Cohen and Mario Lopez.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.560
Y'all have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

